{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794303341855,"sessionID":"ses_e3b3ca287ffeW1XfQqh9dYPxo0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_6D9LpCmNqXl2BN6Eh5wHqORD","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@\n-from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n+from datetime import UTC, datetime, timedelta\n@@\n-from backend.seed import QUESTIONS\n-\n-\n+from backend.seed import QUESTIONS\n+\n@@\n-            (token_hash, datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()),\n+            (token_hash, datetime.now(UTC).isoformat()),\n@@\n-             (datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(days=30)).isoformat()),\n+             (datetime.now(UTC) + timedelta(days=30)).isoformat()),\n@@\n-            \"submitted_at\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(), \"answers\": review,\n+            \"submitted_at\": datetime.now(UTC).isoformat(), \"answers\": review,\n*** Update File: /workspace/frontend/package.json\n@@\n-    \"build\": \"vite build\"\n+    \"build\": \"tsc --noEmit && vite build\",\n+    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n+    \"lint\": \"eslint .\"\n*** Update File: /workspace/frontend/src/Auth.tsx\n@@\n-  const [created, setCreated] = useState(false);\n@@\n-    try {\n+    let registered = false;\n+    try {\n@@\n-        setCreated(true);\n+        registered = true;\n@@\n-      if (mode === \"register\" && created) setMode(\"login\");\n+      if (registered) { setMode(\"login\"); setError(`Your account is ready. Please sign in: ${errorMessage(error)}`); }\n*** Add File: /workspace/backend/test_app.py\n+import sqlite3\n+import tempfile\n+import unittest\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+from backend.app import create_app\n+\n+\n+class QuizApiTests(unittest.TestCase):\n+    def setUp(self):\n+        self.temp = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\n+        self.addCleanup(self.temp.cleanup)\n+        self.database = str(Path(self.temp.name) / \"quiz.sqlite3\")\n+        self.config = {\"TESTING\": True, \"DATABASE\": self.database, \"ADMIN_PASSWORD\": \"test-admin-password\"}\n+        self.app = create_app(self.config)\n+        self.client = self.app.test_client()\n+\n+    def account(self, username=\"alice\"):\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\": username, \"password\": \"strong-password\"})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 201)\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": username, \"password\": \"strong-password\"})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        return {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + response.json[\"token\"]}\n+\n+    def admin(self):\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"test-admin-password\"})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        return {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + response.json[\"token\"]}\n+\n+    def answers(self):\n+        return [{\"question_id\": 1, \"selected\": \"B\"}, {\"question_id\": 2, \"selected\": \"A\"}]\n+\n+    def test_health_and_unknown_api(self):\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/health\").json, {\"status\": \"ok\"})\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/not-found\").status_code, 404)\n+        self.assertIsInstance(self.client.get(\"/api/not-found\").json[\"error\"], str)\n+\n+    def test_seed_draw_and_no_answer_leak(self):\n+        questions = self.client.get(\"/api/quiz?count=50\").json[\"items\"]\n+        self.assertGreaterEqual(len(questions), 20)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(questions), len({question[\"id\"] for question in questions}))\n+        self.assertEqual(len(self.client.get(\"/api/quiz\").json[\"items\"]), 5)\n+        for question in questions:\n+            self.assertEqual(set(question), {\"id\", \"text\", \"option_a\", \"option_b\", \"option_c\", \"option_d\"})\n+\n+    def test_count_validation(self):\n+        for value in [\"0\", \"-1\", \"51\", \"abc\", \"2.5\", \"\", \"9\" * 100]:\n+            with self.subTest(count=value):\n+                self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/quiz\", query_string={\"count\": value}).status_code, 400)\n+\n+    def test_registration_login_and_password_hashing(self):\n+        headers = self.account()\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/auth/me\", headers=headers).json, {\"username\": \"alice\", \"is_admin\": False})\n+        with sqlite3.connect(self.database) as db:\n+            password_hash = db.execute(\"SELECT password_hash FROM users WHERE username = 'alice'\").fetchone()[0]\n+            token_hash = db.execute(\"SELECT token_hash FROM sessions\").fetchone()[0]\n+        self.assertNotEqual(password_hash, \"strong-password\")\n+        self.assertNotIn(token_hash, headers[\"Authorization\"])\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\": \"ALICE\", \"password\": \"strong-password\"}).status_code, 409)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"alice\", \"password\": \"wrong\"}).status_code, 401)\n+\n+    def test_invalid_registration_and_reserved_admin(self):\n+        for value in [None, [], {}, {\"username\": \"a\", \"password\": \"short\"}, {\"username\": [\"name\"], \"password\": \"strong-password\"}]:\n+            self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json=value).status_code, 400)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\": \"Admin\", \"password\": \"strong-password\"}).status_code, 409)\n+\n+    def test_anonymous_score_and_review(self):\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": self.answers()})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        attempt = response.json\n+        self.assertIsNone(attempt[\"id\"])\n+        self.assertEqual((attempt[\"score\"], attempt[\"correct\"], attempt[\"total_questions\"]), (50, 1, 2))\n+        self.assertTrue(attempt[\"answers\"][0][\"is_correct\"])\n+        self.assertFalse(attempt[\"answers\"][1][\"is_correct\"])\n+        self.assertEqual(attempt[\"answers\"][1][\"correct_option\"], \"D\")\n+        self.assertIn(\"text\", attempt[\"answers\"][0])\n+        with sqlite3.connect(self.database) as db:\n+            self.assertEqual(db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM attempts\").fetchone()[0], 0)\n+\n+    def test_attempt_validation(self):\n+        invalid = [None, [], {}, {\"answers\": []}, {\"answers\": \"bad\"}, {\"answers\": [None]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": True, \"selected\": \"A\"}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": 10**100, \"selected\": \"A\"}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": 1, \"selected\": \"E\"}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": 1, \"selected\": [\"A\"]}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": 9999, \"selected\": \"A\"}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [self.answers()[0], self.answers()[0]]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [self.answers()[0]] * 51}]\n+        for value in invalid:\n+            with self.subTest(value=value):\n+                self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json=value).status_code, 400)\n+\n+    def test_history_ownership_and_order(self):\n+        alice = self.account()\n+        first = self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": self.answers()}, headers=alice).json\n+        second = self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": self.answers()}, headers=alice).json\n+        self.assertIsInstance(first[\"id\"], int)\n+        items = self.client.get(\"/api/attempts\", headers=alice).json[\"items\"]\n+        self.assertEqual([item[\"id\"] for item in items], [second[\"id\"], first[\"id\"]])\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(f\"/api/attempts/{first['id']}\", headers=alice).json, first)\n+        bob = self.account(\"bobby\")\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/attempts\", headers=bob).json, {\"items\": []})\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(f\"/api/attempts/{first['id']}\", headers=bob).status_code, 404)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/attempts/999999\", headers=alice).status_code, 404)\n+\n+    def test_authentication_and_authorization(self):\n+        for path in [\"/api/attempts\", \"/api/attempts/1\", \"/api/admin/questions\", \"/api/auth/me\"]:\n+            self.assertEqual(self.client.get(path).status_code, 401)\n+            self.assertEqual(self.client.get(path, headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer invalid\"}).status_code, 401)\n+        alice = self.account()\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=alice).status_code, 403)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=alice, json={}).status_code, 403)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", headers={\"Authorization\": \"Basic invalid\"}, json={\"answers\": self.answers()}).status_code, 401)\n+\n+    def test_admin_create_validate_and_paginate(self):\n+        admin = self.admin()\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=admin, json={})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 400)\n+        self.assertEqual(set(response.json[\"errors\"]), {\"text\", \"option_a\", \"option_b\", \"option_c\", \"option_d\", \"correct_option\"})\n+        question = {\"text\": \"  What is 2 + 2?  \", \"option_a\": \"1\", \"option_b\": \"2\", \"option_c\": \"3\", \"option_d\": \"4\", \"correct_option\": \"D\"}\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/admin/questions\", json=question, headers=admin)\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 201)\n+        self.assertEqual(response.json[\"text\"], \"What is 2 + 2?\")\n+        self.assertEqual(response.json[\"correct_option\"], \"D\")\n+        first = self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions?page=1&page_size=7\", headers=admin).json\n+        second = self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions?page=2&page_size=7\", headers=admin).json\n+        self.assertEqual(first[\"total\"], 31)\n+        self.assertEqual((first[\"page\"], first[\"page_size\"], len(first[\"items\"])), (1, 7, 7))\n+        self.assertTrue({item[\"id\"] for item in first[\"items\"]}.isdisjoint(item[\"id\"] for item in second[\"items\"]))\n+        for query in [\"page=0\", \"page_size=101\", \"page_size=0\", \"page=abc\"]:\n+            self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions?\" + query, headers=admin).status_code, 400)\n+\n+    def test_inactive_questions_excluded(self):\n+        admin = self.admin()\n+        question = {\"text\": \"Inactive?\", \"option_a\": \"A\", \"option_b\": \"B\", \"option_c\": \"C\", \"option_d\": \"D\", \"correct_option\": \"A\", \"active\": False}\n+        created = self.client.post(\"/api/admin/questions\", json=question, headers=admin).json\n+        drawn = self.client.get(\"/api/quiz?count=50\").json[\"items\"]\n+        self.assertNotIn(created[\"id\"], [item[\"id\"] for item in drawn])\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": created[\"id\"], \"selected\": \"A\"}]}).status_code, 400)\n+        listed = self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=admin).json[\"items\"]\n+        self.assertIn(created[\"id\"], [item[\"id\"] for item in listed])\n+\n+    def test_restart_persistence_and_review_snapshot(self):\n+        alice = self.account()\n+        attempt = self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": self.answers()}, headers=alice).json\n+        with sqlite3.connect(self.database) as db:\n+            db.execute(\"UPDATE questions SET text = 'Changed later', correct_option = 'A' WHERE id = 1\")\n+        restarted = create_app(self.config).test_client()\n+        self.assertEqual(restarted.get(f\"/api/attempts/{attempt['id']}\", headers=alice).json, attempt)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(restarted.get(\"/api/quiz?count=50\").json[\"items\"]), 30)\n+\n+    def test_disabled_admin_and_password_rotation(self):\n+        admin = self.admin()\n+        disabled = create_app({**self.config, \"ADMIN_PASSWORD\": \"\"}).test_client()\n+        self.assertEqual(disabled.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"test-admin-password\"}).status_code, 401)\n+        self.assertEqual(disabled.get(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=admin).status_code, 401)\n+        rotated = create_app({**self.config, \"ADMIN_PASSWORD\": \"new-admin-password\"}).test_client()\n+        self.assertEqual(rotated.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"test-admin-password\"}).status_code, 401)\n+        self.assertEqual(rotated.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"new-admin-password\"}).status_code, 200)\n+\n+    def test_logout_and_expiration(self):\n+        alice = self.account()\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/logout\", headers=alice).status_code, 200)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/auth/me\", headers=alice).status_code, 401)\n+        alice = self.client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"alice\", \"password\": \"strong-password\"}).json\n+        with sqlite3.connect(self.database) as db:\n+            db.execute(\"UPDATE sessions SET expires_at = '2000-01-01'\")\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/attempts\", headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + alice[\"token\"]}).status_code, 401)\n+\n+    def test_malformed_json_and_request_limits(self):\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", data=\"{broken\", content_type=\"application/json\").status_code, 400)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", data=\"x\" * 300000, content_type=\"application/json\").status_code, 413)\n+\n+\n+if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n+    unittest.main()\n*** Update File: /workspace/README.md\n@@\n-# App\n+# Quizly\n@@\n-Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n+Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). Update the appropriate lock file when changing dependencies.\n+\n+## Run\n+\n+```sh\n+docker build -t quizly .\n+docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" -e ADMIN_PASSWORD quizly\n+```\n+\n+Set `ADMIN_PASSWORD` in your environment before starting the container to enable the `admin` account. An unset or empty value disables admin sign-in; there is no default password. The SQLite database is initialized with 30 general-knowledge questions on first start. Mount `/app/data` to retain accounts, sessions, questions, and attempts across container replacements.\n+\n+## Local development\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv .venv\n+.venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.lock\n+npm --prefix frontend ci\n+npm --prefix frontend run build\n+.venv/bin/gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 backend.app:app\n+```\n+\n+For frontend hot reloading, run `npm --prefix frontend run dev` alongside the backend. Vite proxies `/api` to port 8000. `DATA_DIR` optionally changes the database directory, which defaults to `./data`.\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+```sh\n+.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s backend -p 'test_*.py' -v\n+.venv/bin/ruff check backend\n+npm --prefix frontend run lint\n+npm --prefix frontend run typecheck\n+npm --prefix frontend run build\n+```\n+\n+Install the optional Python lint tool with `.venv/bin/pip install ruff`.\n+\n+## API notes\n+\n+Register with a username of 3–32 letters, numbers, or underscores and a password of 8–128 characters. Login returns a bearer token valid for 30 days. Passwords are hashed; only token digests are stored. `GET /api/auth/me` restores the signed-in profile; `POST /api/auth/logout` revokes the current token.\n+\n+Quiz draws default to 5 questions and accept `count` from 1 to 50, returning up to the number of active questions available. Submission accepts 1–50 distinct answers. `score` is a percentage, and `correct` is the number of correct answers. Anonymous attempts have a null `id` and are not persisted. Signing in from a guest result saves that result to the account. Saved reviews preserve the question and options as they were submitted.\n+\n+Admin listing defaults to page 1 with 10 questions, with `page_size` up to 100. New questions are active by default; the API also accepts `active: false`. Validation failures return a JSON `error` and, for account creation and question creation, field-specific `errors`.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM backend/app.py\nM frontend/package.json\nM frontend/src/Auth.tsx\nA backend/test_app.py\nM README.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -3,9 +3,9 @@\n import os\n import re\n import secrets\n import sqlite3\n-from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n+from datetime import UTC, datetime, timedelta\n from functools import wraps\n from pathlib import Path\n \n from flask import Flask, g, request, send_from_directory\n@@ -13,9 +13,8 @@\n from werkzeug.security import check_password_hash, generate_password_hash\n \n from backend.seed import QUESTIONS\n \n-\n DIST = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"frontend\" / \"dist\"\n QUESTION_FIELDS = (\n     \"id\", \"text\", \"option_a\", \"option_b\", \"option_c\", \"option_d\", \"correct_option\"\n )\n@@ -128,9 +127,9 @@\n             return fail(\"A valid bearer token is required.\", 401)\n         token_hash = hashlib.sha256(parts[1].encode()).hexdigest()\n         g.user = db().execute(\n             \"SELECT users.* FROM sessions JOIN users ON users.id = sessions.user_id WHERE token_hash = ? AND expires_at > ?\",\n-            (token_hash, datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()),\n+            (token_hash, datetime.now(UTC).isoformat()),\n         ).fetchone()\n         if g.user is None or (g.user[\"is_admin\"] and not app.config[\"ADMIN_PASSWORD\"]):\n             return fail(\"Your session has expired. Please sign in again.\", 401)\n         g.token_hash = token_hash\n@@ -213,9 +212,9 @@\n         token = secrets.token_urlsafe(32)\n         db().execute(\n             \"INSERT INTO sessions VALUES (?, ?, ?)\",\n             (hashlib.sha256(token.encode()).hexdigest(), user[\"id\"],\n-             (datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(days=30)).isoformat()),\n+             (datetime.now(UTC) + timedelta(days=30)).isoformat()),\n         )\n         db().commit()\n         return {\"token\": token, \"user\": user_json(user)}\n \n@@ -268,9 +267,9 @@\n         correct = sum(answer[\"is_correct\"] for answer in review)\n         result = {\n             \"id\": None, \"score\": round(correct / len(review) * 100, 2),\n             \"correct\": correct, \"total_questions\": len(review),\n-            \"submitted_at\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(), \"answers\": review,\n+            \"submitted_at\": datetime.now(UTC).isoformat(), \"answers\": review,\n         }\n         if g.user is not None:\n             cursor = db().execute(\n                 \"INSERT INTO attempts (user_id, score, correct, total_questions, submitted_at, answers) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n\nIndex: /workspace/frontend/package.json\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/package.json\n+++ /workspace/frontend/package.json\n@@ -3,9 +3,11 @@\n \"private\": true,\n \"type\": \"module\",\n \"scripts\": {\n   \"dev\": \"vite\",\n-  \"build\": \"vite build\"\n+  \"build\": \"tsc --noEmit && vite build\",\n+  \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n+  \"lint\": \"eslint .\"\n },\n \"dependencies\": {\n   \"react\": \"19.3.1\",\n   \"react-dom\": \"19.3.1\"\n\nIndex: /workspace/frontend/src/Auth.tsx\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/Auth.tsx\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/Auth.tsx\n@@ -11,24 +11,24 @@\n const [password, setPassword] = useState(\"\");\n const [error, setError] = useState(\"\");\n const [fields, setFields] = useState<Record<string, string>>({});\n const [busy, setBusy] = useState(false);\n-const [created, setCreated] = useState(false);\n async function submit(event: FormEvent) {\n   event.preventDefault();\n   setBusy(true); setError(\"\"); setFields({});\n+  let registered = false;\n   try {\n     if (mode === \"register\") {\n       await api(\"/auth/register\", { method: \"POST\", body: JSON.stringify({ username, password }) });\n-      setCreated(true);\n+      registered = true;\n     }\n     const result = await api<{ token: string; user: User }>(\"/auth/login\", { method: \"POST\", body: JSON.stringify({ username, password }) });\n     setToken(result.token);\n     onSuccess(result.user);\n   } catch (error) {\n     setError(errorMessage(error));\n     if (error instanceof ApiError) setFields(error.fields);\n-    if (mode === \"register\" && created) setMode(\"login\");\n+    if (registered) { setMode(\"login\"); setError(`Your account is ready. Please sign in: ${errorMessage(error)}`); }\n   } finally { setBusy(false); }\n }\n return <Modal onClose={onClose} title={mode === \"login\" ? \"Sign in to Quizly\" : \"Create your Quizly account\"}>\n   <span className=\"mb-7 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-lime\"><Icon name=\"spark\" size={28} /></span>\n\nIndex: /workspace/backend/test_app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/test_app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/test_app.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,176 @@\n+import sqlite3\n+import tempfile\n+import unittest\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+from backend.app import create_app\n+\n+\n+class QuizApiTests(unittest.TestCase):\n+    def setUp(self):\n+        self.temp = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\n+        self.addCleanup(self.temp.cleanup)\n+        self.database = str(Path(self.temp.name) / \"quiz.sqlite3\")\n+        self.config = {\"TESTING\": True, \"DATABASE\": self.database, \"ADMIN_PASSWORD\": \"test-admin-password\"}\n+        self.app = create_app(self.config)\n+        self.client = self.app.test_client()\n+\n+    def account(self, username=\"alice\"):\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\": username, \"password\": \"strong-password\"})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 201)\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": username, \"password\": \"strong-password\"})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        return {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + response.json[\"token\"]}\n+\n+    def admin(self):\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"test-admin-password\"})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        return {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + response.json[\"token\"]}\n+\n+    def answers(self):\n+        return [{\"question_id\": 1, \"selected\": \"B\"}, {\"question_id\": 2, \"selected\": \"A\"}]\n+\n+    def test_health_and_unknown_api(self):\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/health\").json, {\"status\": \"ok\"})\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/not-found\").status_code, 404)\n+        self.assertIsInstance(self.client.get(\"/api/not-found\").json[\"error\"], str)\n+\n+    def test_seed_draw_and_no_answer_leak(self):\n+        questions = self.client.get(\"/api/quiz?count=50\").json[\"items\"]\n+        self.assertGreaterEqual(len(questions), 20)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(questions), len({question[\"id\"] for question in questions}))\n+        self.assertEqual(len(self.client.get(\"/api/quiz\").json[\"items\"]), 5)\n+        for question in questions:\n+            self.assertEqual(set(question), {\"id\", \"text\", \"option_a\", \"option_b\", \"option_c\", \"option_d\"})\n+\n+    def test_count_validation(self):\n+        for value in [\"0\", \"-1\", \"51\", \"abc\", \"2.5\", \"\", \"9\" * 100]:\n+            with self.subTest(count=value):\n+                self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/quiz\", query_string={\"count\": value}).status_code, 400)\n+\n+    def test_registration_login_and_password_hashing(self):\n+        headers = self.account()\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/auth/me\", headers=headers).json, {\"username\": \"alice\", \"is_admin\": False})\n+        with sqlite3.connect(self.database) as db:\n+            password_hash = db.execute(\"SELECT password_hash FROM users WHERE username = 'alice'\").fetchone()[0]\n+            token_hash = db.execute(\"SELECT token_hash FROM sessions\").fetchone()[0]\n+        self.assertNotEqual(password_hash, \"strong-password\")\n+        self.assertNotIn(token_hash, headers[\"Authorization\"])\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\": \"ALICE\", \"password\": \"strong-password\"}).status_code, 409)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"alice\", \"password\": \"wrong\"}).status_code, 401)\n+\n+    def test_invalid_registration_and_reserved_admin(self):\n+        for value in [None, [], {}, {\"username\": \"a\", \"password\": \"short\"}, {\"username\": [\"name\"], \"password\": \"strong-password\"}]:\n+            self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json=value).status_code, 400)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\": \"Admin\", \"password\": \"strong-password\"}).status_code, 409)\n+\n+    def test_anonymous_score_and_review(self):\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": self.answers()})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        attempt = response.json\n+        self.assertIsNone(attempt[\"id\"])\n+        self.assertEqual((attempt[\"score\"], attempt[\"correct\"], attempt[\"total_questions\"]), (50, 1, 2))\n+        self.assertTrue(attempt[\"answers\"][0][\"is_correct\"])\n+        self.assertFalse(attempt[\"answers\"][1][\"is_correct\"])\n+        self.assertEqual(attempt[\"answers\"][1][\"correct_option\"], \"D\")\n+        self.assertIn(\"text\", attempt[\"answers\"][0])\n+        with sqlite3.connect(self.database) as db:\n+            self.assertEqual(db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM attempts\").fetchone()[0], 0)\n+\n+    def test_attempt_validation(self):\n+        invalid = [None, [], {}, {\"answers\": []}, {\"answers\": \"bad\"}, {\"answers\": [None]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": True, \"selected\": \"A\"}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": 10**100, \"selected\": \"A\"}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": 1, \"selected\": \"E\"}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": 1, \"selected\": [\"A\"]}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": 9999, \"selected\": \"A\"}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [self.answers()[0], self.answers()[0]]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [self.answers()[0]] * 51}]\n+        for value in invalid:\n+            with self.subTest(value=value):\n+                self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json=value).status_code, 400)\n+\n+    def test_history_ownership_and_order(self):\n+        alice = self.account()\n+        first = self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": self.answers()}, headers=alice).json\n+        second = self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": self.answers()}, headers=alice).json\n+        self.assertIsInstance(first[\"id\"], int)\n+        items = self.client.get(\"/api/attempts\", headers=alice).json[\"items\"]\n+        self.assertEqual([item[\"id\"] for item in items], [second[\"id\"], first[\"id\"]])\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(f\"/api/attempts/{first['id']}\", headers=alice).json, first)\n+        bob = self.account(\"bobby\")\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/attempts\", headers=bob).json, {\"items\": []})\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(f\"/api/attempts/{first['id']}\", headers=bob).status_code, 404)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/attempts/999999\", headers=alice).status_code, 404)\n+\n+    def test_authentication_and_authorization(self):\n+        for path in [\"/api/attempts\", \"/api/attempts/1\", \"/api/admin/questions\", \"/api/auth/me\"]:\n+            self.assertEqual(self.client.get(path).status_code, 401)\n+            self.assertEqual(self.client.get(path, headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer invalid\"}).status_code, 401)\n+        alice = self.account()\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=alice).status_code, 403)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=alice, json={}).status_code, 403)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", headers={\"Authorization\": \"Basic invalid\"}, json={\"answers\": self.answers()}).status_code, 401)\n+\n+    def test_admin_create_validate_and_paginate(self):\n+        admin = self.admin()\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=admin, json={})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 400)\n+        self.assertEqual(set(response.json[\"errors\"]), {\"text\", \"option_a\", \"option_b\", \"option_c\", \"option_d\", \"correct_option\"})\n+        question = {\"text\": \"  What is 2 + 2?  \", \"option_a\": \"1\", \"option_b\": \"2\", \"option_c\": \"3\", \"option_d\": \"4\", \"correct_option\": \"D\"}\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/admin/questions\", json=question, headers=admin)\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 201)\n+        self.assertEqual(response.json[\"text\"], \"What is 2 + 2?\")\n+        self.assertEqual(response.json[\"correct_option\"], \"D\")\n+        first = self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions?page=1&page_size=7\", headers=admin).json\n+        second = self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions?page=2&page_size=7\", headers=admin).json\n+        self.assertEqual(first[\"total\"], 31)\n+        self.assertEqual((first[\"page\"], first[\"page_size\"], len(first[\"items\"])), (1, 7, 7))\n+        self.assertTrue({item[\"id\"] for item in first[\"items\"]}.isdisjoint(item[\"id\"] for item in second[\"items\"]))\n+        for query in [\"page=0\", \"page_size=101\", \"page_size=0\", \"page=abc\"]:\n+            self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions?\" + query, headers=admin).status_code, 400)\n+\n+    def test_inactive_questions_excluded(self):\n+        admin = self.admin()\n+        question = {\"text\": \"Inactive?\", \"option_a\": \"A\", \"option_b\": \"B\", \"option_c\": \"C\", \"option_d\": \"D\", \"correct_option\": \"A\", \"active\": False}\n+        created = self.client.post(\"/api/admin/questions\", json=question, headers=admin).json\n+        drawn = self.client.get(\"/api/quiz?count=50\").json[\"items\"]\n+        self.assertNotIn(created[\"id\"], [item[\"id\"] for item in drawn])\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": created[\"id\"], \"selected\": \"A\"}]}).status_code, 400)\n+        listed = self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=admin).json[\"items\"]\n+        self.assertIn(created[\"id\"], [item[\"id\"] for item in listed])\n+\n+    def test_restart_persistence_and_review_snapshot(self):\n+        alice = self.account()\n+        attempt = self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": self.answers()}, headers=alice).json\n+        with sqlite3.connect(self.database) as db:\n+            db.execute(\"UPDATE questions SET text = 'Changed later', correct_option = 'A' WHERE id = 1\")\n+        restarted = create_app(self.config).test_client()\n+        self.assertEqual(restarted.get(f\"/api/attempts/{attempt['id']}\", headers=alice).json, attempt)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(restarted.get(\"/api/quiz?count=50\").json[\"items\"]), 30)\n+\n+    def test_disabled_admin_and_password_rotation(self):\n+        admin = self.admin()\n+        disabled = create_app({**self.config, \"ADMIN_PASSWORD\": \"\"}).test_client()\n+        self.assertEqual(disabled.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"test-admin-password\"}).status_code, 401)\n+        self.assertEqual(disabled.get(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=admin).status_code, 401)\n+        rotated = create_app({**self.config, \"ADMIN_PASSWORD\": \"new-admin-password\"}).test_client()\n+        self.assertEqual(rotated.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"test-admin-password\"}).status_code, 401)\n+        self.assertEqual(rotated.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"new-admin-password\"}).status_code, 200)\n+\n+    def test_logout_and_expiration(self):\n+        alice = self.account()\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/logout\", headers=alice).status_code, 200)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/auth/me\", headers=alice).status_code, 401)\n+        alice = self.client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"alice\", \"password\": \"strong-password\"}).json\n+        with sqlite3.connect(self.database) as db:\n+            db.execute(\"UPDATE sessions SET expires_at = '2000-01-01'\")\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/attempts\", headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + alice[\"token\"]}).status_code, 401)\n+\n+    def test_malformed_json_and_request_limits(self):\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", data=\"{broken\", content_type=\"application/json\").status_code, 400)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", data=\"x\" * 300000, content_type=\"application/json\").status_code, 413)\n+\n+\n+if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n+    unittest.main()\n\nIndex: /workspace/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/README.md\n+++ /workspace/README.md\n@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@\n-# App\n+# Quizly\n \n ## Run contract\n \n - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n@@ -11,5 +11,46 @@\n \n - `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n \n-Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n+Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). Update the appropriate lock file when changing dependencies.\n+\n+## Run\n+\n+```sh\n+docker build -t quizly .\n+docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" -e ADMIN_PASSWORD quizly\n+```\n+\n+Set `ADMIN_PASSWORD` in your environment before starting the container to enable the `admin` account. An unset or empty value disables admin sign-in; there is no default password. The SQLite database is initialized with 30 general-knowledge questions on first start. Mount `/app/data` to retain accounts, sessions, questions, and attempts across container replacements.\n+\n+## Local development\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv .venv\n+.venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.lock\n+npm --prefix frontend ci\n+npm --prefix frontend run build\n+.venv/bin/gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 backend.app:app\n+```\n+\n+For frontend hot reloading, run `npm --prefix frontend run dev` alongside the backend. Vite proxies `/api` to port 8000. `DATA_DIR` optionally changes the database directory, which defaults to `./data`.\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+```sh\n+.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s backend -p 'test_*.py' -v\n+.venv/bin/ruff check backend\n+npm --prefix frontend run lint\n+npm --prefix frontend run typecheck\n+npm --prefix frontend run build\n+```\n+\n+Install the optional Python lint tool with `.venv/bin/pip install ruff`.\n+\n+## API notes\n+\n+Register with a username of 3–32 letters, numbers, or underscores and a password of 8–128 characters. Login returns a bearer token valid for 30 days. Passwords are hashed; only token digests are stored. `GET /api/auth/me` restores the signed-in profile; `POST /api/auth/logout` revokes the current token.\n+\n+Quiz draws default to 5 questions and accept `count` from 1 to 50, returning up to the number of active questions available. Submission accepts 1–50 distinct answers. `score` is a percentage, and `correct` is the number of correct answers. Anonymous attempts have a null `id` and are not persisted. Signing in from a guest result saves that result to the account. Saved reviews preserve the question and options as they were submitted.\n+\n+Admin listing defaults to page 1 with 10 questions, with `page_size` up to 100. New questions are active by default; the API also accepts `active: false`. Validation failures return a JSON `error` and, for account creation and question creation, field-specific `errors`.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/app.py","relativePath":"backend/app.py","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/app.py\n@@ -3,9 +3,9 @@\n import os\n import re\n import secrets\n import sqlite3\n-from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n+from datetime import UTC, datetime, timedelta\n from functools import wraps\n from pathlib import Path\n \n from flask import Flask, g, request, send_from_directory\n@@ -13,9 +13,8 @@\n from werkzeug.security import check_password_hash, generate_password_hash\n \n from backend.seed import QUESTIONS\n \n-\n DIST = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"frontend\" / \"dist\"\n QUESTION_FIELDS = (\n     \"id\", \"text\", \"option_a\", \"option_b\", \"option_c\", \"option_d\", \"correct_option\"\n )\n@@ -128,9 +127,9 @@\n             return fail(\"A valid bearer token is required.\", 401)\n         token_hash = hashlib.sha256(parts[1].encode()).hexdigest()\n         g.user = db().execute(\n             \"SELECT users.* FROM sessions JOIN users ON users.id = sessions.user_id WHERE token_hash = ? AND expires_at > ?\",\n-            (token_hash, datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()),\n+            (token_hash, datetime.now(UTC).isoformat()),\n         ).fetchone()\n         if g.user is None or (g.user[\"is_admin\"] and not app.config[\"ADMIN_PASSWORD\"]):\n             return fail(\"Your session has expired. Please sign in again.\", 401)\n         g.token_hash = token_hash\n@@ -213,9 +212,9 @@\n         token = secrets.token_urlsafe(32)\n         db().execute(\n             \"INSERT INTO sessions VALUES (?, ?, ?)\",\n             (hashlib.sha256(token.encode()).hexdigest(), user[\"id\"],\n-             (datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(days=30)).isoformat()),\n+             (datetime.now(UTC) + timedelta(days=30)).isoformat()),\n         )\n         db().commit()\n         return {\"token\": token, \"user\": user_json(user)}\n \n@@ -268,9 +267,9 @@\n         correct = sum(answer[\"is_correct\"] for answer in review)\n         result = {\n             \"id\": None, \"score\": round(correct / len(review) * 100, 2),\n             \"correct\": correct, \"total_questions\": len(review),\n-            \"submitted_at\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(), \"answers\": review,\n+            \"submitted_at\": datetime.now(UTC).isoformat(), \"answers\": review,\n         }\n         if g.user is not None:\n             cursor = db().execute(\n                 \"INSERT INTO attempts (user_id, score, correct, total_questions, submitted_at, answers) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n","additions":4,"deletions":5},{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/package.json","relativePath":"frontend/package.json","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/frontend/package.json\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/package.json\n+++ /workspace/frontend/package.json\n@@ -3,9 +3,11 @@\n \"private\": true,\n \"type\": \"module\",\n \"scripts\": {\n   \"dev\": \"vite\",\n-  \"build\": \"vite build\"\n+  \"build\": \"tsc --noEmit && vite build\",\n+  \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n+  \"lint\": \"eslint .\"\n },\n \"dependencies\": {\n   \"react\": \"19.3.1\",\n   \"react-dom\": \"19.3.1\"\n","additions":3,"deletions":1},{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/Auth.tsx","relativePath":"frontend/src/Auth.tsx","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/Auth.tsx\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/Auth.tsx\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/Auth.tsx\n@@ -11,24 +11,24 @@\n const [password, setPassword] = useState(\"\");\n const [error, setError] = useState(\"\");\n const [fields, setFields] = useState<Record<string, string>>({});\n const [busy, setBusy] = useState(false);\n-const [created, setCreated] = useState(false);\n async function submit(event: FormEvent) {\n   event.preventDefault();\n   setBusy(true); setError(\"\"); setFields({});\n+  let registered = false;\n   try {\n     if (mode === \"register\") {\n       await api(\"/auth/register\", { method: \"POST\", body: JSON.stringify({ username, password }) });\n-      setCreated(true);\n+      registered = true;\n     }\n     const result = await api<{ token: string; user: User }>(\"/auth/login\", { method: \"POST\", body: JSON.stringify({ username, password }) });\n     setToken(result.token);\n     onSuccess(result.user);\n   } catch (error) {\n     setError(errorMessage(error));\n     if (error instanceof ApiError) setFields(error.fields);\n-    if (mode === \"register\" && created) setMode(\"login\");\n+    if (registered) { setMode(\"login\"); setError(`Your account is ready. Please sign in: ${errorMessage(error)}`); }\n   } finally { setBusy(false); }\n }\n return <Modal onClose={onClose} title={mode === \"login\" ? \"Sign in to Quizly\" : \"Create your Quizly account\"}>\n   <span className=\"mb-7 flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-lime\"><Icon name=\"spark\" size={28} /></span>\n","additions":3,"deletions":3},{"filePath":"/workspace/backend/test_app.py","relativePath":"backend/test_app.py","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/backend/test_app.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/backend/test_app.py\n+++ /workspace/backend/test_app.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,176 @@\n+import sqlite3\n+import tempfile\n+import unittest\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+from backend.app import create_app\n+\n+\n+class QuizApiTests(unittest.TestCase):\n+    def setUp(self):\n+        self.temp = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\n+        self.addCleanup(self.temp.cleanup)\n+        self.database = str(Path(self.temp.name) / \"quiz.sqlite3\")\n+        self.config = {\"TESTING\": True, \"DATABASE\": self.database, \"ADMIN_PASSWORD\": \"test-admin-password\"}\n+        self.app = create_app(self.config)\n+        self.client = self.app.test_client()\n+\n+    def account(self, username=\"alice\"):\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\": username, \"password\": \"strong-password\"})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 201)\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": username, \"password\": \"strong-password\"})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        return {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + response.json[\"token\"]}\n+\n+    def admin(self):\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"test-admin-password\"})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        return {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + response.json[\"token\"]}\n+\n+    def answers(self):\n+        return [{\"question_id\": 1, \"selected\": \"B\"}, {\"question_id\": 2, \"selected\": \"A\"}]\n+\n+    def test_health_and_unknown_api(self):\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/health\").json, {\"status\": \"ok\"})\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/not-found\").status_code, 404)\n+        self.assertIsInstance(self.client.get(\"/api/not-found\").json[\"error\"], str)\n+\n+    def test_seed_draw_and_no_answer_leak(self):\n+        questions = self.client.get(\"/api/quiz?count=50\").json[\"items\"]\n+        self.assertGreaterEqual(len(questions), 20)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(questions), len({question[\"id\"] for question in questions}))\n+        self.assertEqual(len(self.client.get(\"/api/quiz\").json[\"items\"]), 5)\n+        for question in questions:\n+            self.assertEqual(set(question), {\"id\", \"text\", \"option_a\", \"option_b\", \"option_c\", \"option_d\"})\n+\n+    def test_count_validation(self):\n+        for value in [\"0\", \"-1\", \"51\", \"abc\", \"2.5\", \"\", \"9\" * 100]:\n+            with self.subTest(count=value):\n+                self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/quiz\", query_string={\"count\": value}).status_code, 400)\n+\n+    def test_registration_login_and_password_hashing(self):\n+        headers = self.account()\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/auth/me\", headers=headers).json, {\"username\": \"alice\", \"is_admin\": False})\n+        with sqlite3.connect(self.database) as db:\n+            password_hash = db.execute(\"SELECT password_hash FROM users WHERE username = 'alice'\").fetchone()[0]\n+            token_hash = db.execute(\"SELECT token_hash FROM sessions\").fetchone()[0]\n+        self.assertNotEqual(password_hash, \"strong-password\")\n+        self.assertNotIn(token_hash, headers[\"Authorization\"])\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\": \"ALICE\", \"password\": \"strong-password\"}).status_code, 409)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"alice\", \"password\": \"wrong\"}).status_code, 401)\n+\n+    def test_invalid_registration_and_reserved_admin(self):\n+        for value in [None, [], {}, {\"username\": \"a\", \"password\": \"short\"}, {\"username\": [\"name\"], \"password\": \"strong-password\"}]:\n+            self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json=value).status_code, 400)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\": \"Admin\", \"password\": \"strong-password\"}).status_code, 409)\n+\n+    def test_anonymous_score_and_review(self):\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": self.answers()})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 200)\n+        attempt = response.json\n+        self.assertIsNone(attempt[\"id\"])\n+        self.assertEqual((attempt[\"score\"], attempt[\"correct\"], attempt[\"total_questions\"]), (50, 1, 2))\n+        self.assertTrue(attempt[\"answers\"][0][\"is_correct\"])\n+        self.assertFalse(attempt[\"answers\"][1][\"is_correct\"])\n+        self.assertEqual(attempt[\"answers\"][1][\"correct_option\"], \"D\")\n+        self.assertIn(\"text\", attempt[\"answers\"][0])\n+        with sqlite3.connect(self.database) as db:\n+            self.assertEqual(db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM attempts\").fetchone()[0], 0)\n+\n+    def test_attempt_validation(self):\n+        invalid = [None, [], {}, {\"answers\": []}, {\"answers\": \"bad\"}, {\"answers\": [None]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": True, \"selected\": \"A\"}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": 10**100, \"selected\": \"A\"}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": 1, \"selected\": \"E\"}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": 1, \"selected\": [\"A\"]}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": 9999, \"selected\": \"A\"}]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [self.answers()[0], self.answers()[0]]},\n+                   {\"answers\": [self.answers()[0]] * 51}]\n+        for value in invalid:\n+            with self.subTest(value=value):\n+                self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json=value).status_code, 400)\n+\n+    def test_history_ownership_and_order(self):\n+        alice = self.account()\n+        first = self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": self.answers()}, headers=alice).json\n+        second = self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": self.answers()}, headers=alice).json\n+        self.assertIsInstance(first[\"id\"], int)\n+        items = self.client.get(\"/api/attempts\", headers=alice).json[\"items\"]\n+        self.assertEqual([item[\"id\"] for item in items], [second[\"id\"], first[\"id\"]])\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(f\"/api/attempts/{first['id']}\", headers=alice).json, first)\n+        bob = self.account(\"bobby\")\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/attempts\", headers=bob).json, {\"items\": []})\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(f\"/api/attempts/{first['id']}\", headers=bob).status_code, 404)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/attempts/999999\", headers=alice).status_code, 404)\n+\n+    def test_authentication_and_authorization(self):\n+        for path in [\"/api/attempts\", \"/api/attempts/1\", \"/api/admin/questions\", \"/api/auth/me\"]:\n+            self.assertEqual(self.client.get(path).status_code, 401)\n+            self.assertEqual(self.client.get(path, headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer invalid\"}).status_code, 401)\n+        alice = self.account()\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=alice).status_code, 403)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=alice, json={}).status_code, 403)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", headers={\"Authorization\": \"Basic invalid\"}, json={\"answers\": self.answers()}).status_code, 401)\n+\n+    def test_admin_create_validate_and_paginate(self):\n+        admin = self.admin()\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=admin, json={})\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 400)\n+        self.assertEqual(set(response.json[\"errors\"]), {\"text\", \"option_a\", \"option_b\", \"option_c\", \"option_d\", \"correct_option\"})\n+        question = {\"text\": \"  What is 2 + 2?  \", \"option_a\": \"1\", \"option_b\": \"2\", \"option_c\": \"3\", \"option_d\": \"4\", \"correct_option\": \"D\"}\n+        response = self.client.post(\"/api/admin/questions\", json=question, headers=admin)\n+        self.assertEqual(response.status_code, 201)\n+        self.assertEqual(response.json[\"text\"], \"What is 2 + 2?\")\n+        self.assertEqual(response.json[\"correct_option\"], \"D\")\n+        first = self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions?page=1&page_size=7\", headers=admin).json\n+        second = self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions?page=2&page_size=7\", headers=admin).json\n+        self.assertEqual(first[\"total\"], 31)\n+        self.assertEqual((first[\"page\"], first[\"page_size\"], len(first[\"items\"])), (1, 7, 7))\n+        self.assertTrue({item[\"id\"] for item in first[\"items\"]}.isdisjoint(item[\"id\"] for item in second[\"items\"]))\n+        for query in [\"page=0\", \"page_size=101\", \"page_size=0\", \"page=abc\"]:\n+            self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions?\" + query, headers=admin).status_code, 400)\n+\n+    def test_inactive_questions_excluded(self):\n+        admin = self.admin()\n+        question = {\"text\": \"Inactive?\", \"option_a\": \"A\", \"option_b\": \"B\", \"option_c\": \"C\", \"option_d\": \"D\", \"correct_option\": \"A\", \"active\": False}\n+        created = self.client.post(\"/api/admin/questions\", json=question, headers=admin).json\n+        drawn = self.client.get(\"/api/quiz?count=50\").json[\"items\"]\n+        self.assertNotIn(created[\"id\"], [item[\"id\"] for item in drawn])\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": [{\"question_id\": created[\"id\"], \"selected\": \"A\"}]}).status_code, 400)\n+        listed = self.client.get(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=admin).json[\"items\"]\n+        self.assertIn(created[\"id\"], [item[\"id\"] for item in listed])\n+\n+    def test_restart_persistence_and_review_snapshot(self):\n+        alice = self.account()\n+        attempt = self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", json={\"answers\": self.answers()}, headers=alice).json\n+        with sqlite3.connect(self.database) as db:\n+            db.execute(\"UPDATE questions SET text = 'Changed later', correct_option = 'A' WHERE id = 1\")\n+        restarted = create_app(self.config).test_client()\n+        self.assertEqual(restarted.get(f\"/api/attempts/{attempt['id']}\", headers=alice).json, attempt)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(restarted.get(\"/api/quiz?count=50\").json[\"items\"]), 30)\n+\n+    def test_disabled_admin_and_password_rotation(self):\n+        admin = self.admin()\n+        disabled = create_app({**self.config, \"ADMIN_PASSWORD\": \"\"}).test_client()\n+        self.assertEqual(disabled.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"test-admin-password\"}).status_code, 401)\n+        self.assertEqual(disabled.get(\"/api/admin/questions\", headers=admin).status_code, 401)\n+        rotated = create_app({**self.config, \"ADMIN_PASSWORD\": \"new-admin-password\"}).test_client()\n+        self.assertEqual(rotated.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"test-admin-password\"}).status_code, 401)\n+        self.assertEqual(rotated.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"new-admin-password\"}).status_code, 200)\n+\n+    def test_logout_and_expiration(self):\n+        alice = self.account()\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/auth/logout\", headers=alice).status_code, 200)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/auth/me\", headers=alice).status_code, 401)\n+        alice = self.client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"alice\", \"password\": \"strong-password\"}).json\n+        with sqlite3.connect(self.database) as db:\n+            db.execute(\"UPDATE sessions SET expires_at = '2000-01-01'\")\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.get(\"/api/attempts\", headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + alice[\"token\"]}).status_code, 401)\n+\n+    def test_malformed_json_and_request_limits(self):\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", data=\"{broken\", content_type=\"application/json\").status_code, 400)\n+        self.assertEqual(self.client.post(\"/api/attempts\", data=\"x\" * 300000, content_type=\"application/json\").status_code, 413)\n+\n+\n+if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n+    unittest.main()\n","additions":176,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md","relativePath":"README.md","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/README.md\n+++ /workspace/README.md\n@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@\n-# App\n+# Quizly\n \n ## Run contract\n \n - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n@@ -11,5 +11,46 @@\n \n - `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n \n-Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n+Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). Update the appropriate lock file when changing dependencies.\n+\n+## Run\n+\n+```sh\n+docker build -t quizly .\n+docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v \"$(pwd)/data:/app/data\" -e ADMIN_PASSWORD quizly\n+```\n+\n+Set `ADMIN_PASSWORD` in your environment before starting the container to enable the `admin` account. An unset or empty value disables admin sign-in; there is no default password. The SQLite database is initialized with 30 general-knowledge questions on first start. Mount `/app/data` to retain accounts, sessions, questions, and attempts across container replacements.\n+\n+## Local development\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv .venv\n+.venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.lock\n+npm --prefix frontend ci\n+npm --prefix frontend run build\n+.venv/bin/gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 backend.app:app\n+```\n+\n+For frontend hot reloading, run `npm --prefix frontend run dev` alongside the backend. Vite proxies `/api` to port 8000. `DATA_DIR` optionally changes the database directory, which defaults to `./data`.\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+```sh\n+.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s backend -p 'test_*.py' -v\n+.venv/bin/ruff check backend\n+npm --prefix frontend run lint\n+npm --prefix frontend run typecheck\n+npm --prefix frontend run build\n+```\n+\n+Install the optional Python lint tool with `.venv/bin/pip install ruff`.\n+\n+## API notes\n+\n+Register with a username of 3–32 letters, numbers, or underscores and a password of 8–128 characters. Login returns a bearer token valid for 30 days. Passwords are hashed; only token digests are stored. `GET /api/auth/me` restores the signed-in profile; `POST /api/auth/logout` revokes the current token.\n+\n+Quiz draws default to 5 questions and accept `count` from 1 to 50, returning up to the number of active questions available. Submission accepts 1–50 distinct answers. `score` is a percentage, and `correct` is the number of correct answers. Anonymous attempts have a null `id` and are not persisted. Signing in from a guest result saves that result to the account. Saved reviews preserve the question and options as they were submitted.\n+\n+Admin listing defaults to page 1 with 10 questions, with `page_size` up to 100. New questions are active by default; the API also accepts `active: false`. Validation failures return a JSON `error` and, for account creation and question creation, field-specific `errors`.\n","additions":43,"deletions":2}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM backend/app.py\nM frontend/package.json\nM frontend/src/Auth.tsx\nA backend/test_app.py\nM README.md","time":{"start":1794303341829,"end":1794303341849}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"gAAAAABq8uVJ9fstku_ZWeJz9Lh3Gpzh9NsiZecg8FcGeT0nZoMHOAb7SN52WB6nd45JG-dmVKQSygZep-2wZunEAaB00fo6446adgp9k_tJvip7h9EEgT6No3K50JLdnpBe3k0eyukzI2OOoQTznF7a0e1v_a-asoO9s4aADE_9PC3o5R0bgHCL5Njqvkeabfu-69Iu0iL0iaH-vkJonm9ZswsFkn60z7XXQo-5IvtUGnJ-qfksPycr_ijWtbdedKg6yB4WwbJGgSpzdhXUXJUJ8763HgmlJO5r7U22hsUGhU-gx8ranKNK59dI008LkFv_51AtSjW41mMO3ExraiuT8dvEHTLScUeqcKwrSsZS8mPk6vglGXGGACSpdV-pmON6bFS7vclirAhCbm5TEYZPQCfTWuQ7QniTDxOyygZOhzY79iHVDQmFKxbp8h903bDPFcRsvQWTmpUgKEHCglJP4fvmfG0v4sfphF68sKjZZufJpMbrPGTpuuHGMsUwDU_AreM1tYUw9k9B-5Jhq5oFFGIRGKJTrnT-T_I0UrnSfDoVb6vwJFNduF8oRMwzxg4YvGZmR_eev6kgKuKc_JkIt-yJNGsKS_sl2tPeTHnalnoP5gDUBnTNIP1lAgHBucQ8GqRDztwsbH2Z3mKU1r_JglKD6Cau8aXvskZAywKI8mcP6M83kOqG9jcK8xlk72UNuOV7gv7twemGy7JS